<section class="chatoyancy-box">
  <h2>🐈 Cat's-eye stones (chatoyancy)</h2>
  <p>Asterism has a single-ray relative. When a stone has only <strong>one</strong> set of parallel needles or fibres, a cabochon shows a single bright band that slides across the dome like light in a cat's eye. The most prized example is chrysoberyl cat's-eye ("cymophane"). Tiger's eye gets its shimmer from fibres replaced by quartz.</p>
